  "definition": "Maximum Likelihood Estimation chooses the parameter values that make the observed data most probable under the assumed model. It is a core estimation principle that connects probabilistic modeling, log-likelihood, and many classical statistical estimators.",
  "intuition": "Pick the parameters that best explain the observed sample under the model.",
  "mathematical_foundation": "$$\n\\hat{\\theta} = \\arg\\max_{\\theta} \\prod_i p(x_i \\mid \\theta)\n$$\n\nOften we maximize the log-likelihood instead:\n\n$$\n\\ell(\\theta) = \\sum_i \\log p(x_i \\mid \\theta)\n$$",
